    <node id="越国">
      <data key="d0">越国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity 越国 (Yue State) refers to an ancient Chinese kingdom prominently associated with its ruler, 越王勾践 (King Goujian). It is historically recognized as the state governed by Goujian, who played a central role in its narrative and conflicts. 越国 was notably engaged in a prolonged rivalry with 吴国 (Wu State), characterized by enmity and warfare, making the two states historical adversaries. This antagonism is a defining feature of 越国's history and is frequently highlighted in accounts of its interactions with Wu.

The state is also closely linked to several notable figures, including 范蠡 (Fan Li), a renowned strategist and advisor, and 文种 (Wen Zhong), another key figure in its administration. Both individuals are celebrated for their contributions to 越国's governance and military strategies. Additionally, 阿青 (A Qing), a lesser-known figure, is mentioned in connection with 越国, further emphasizing the state's historical and cultural significance.

越国 serves as the backdrop for many historical and legendary events, with its struggles against 吴国 forming a central theme. The kingdom's resilience and eventual triumph under Goujian's leadership are often highlighted in historical narratives, symbolizing perseverance and strategic acumen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8283a4a379ab2b74495b2a64a83b7b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1777541096</data>
      <data key="d6" />
